,"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3874939293","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116065#issuecomment-3874939293","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116065","id":3874939293,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7m9uGd","user":{"login":"fakemaxwell","id":59422275,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5NDIyMjc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59422275?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fakemaxwell","html_url":"https://github.com/fakemaxwell","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fakemaxwell/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fakemaxwell/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fakemaxwell/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fakemaxwell/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fakemaxwell/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fakemaxwell/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fakemaxwell/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fakemaxwell/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fakemaxwell/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-10T02:19:47Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T02:19:47Z","body":"After digging into it more, what I believe is happening is that Photoshop and CSP have their alpha pixels as white(00FFFFFF) vs the others are black (00000000). I'm out of my depth, but I think  _generate_po2_mipmap() is not handling these possibilities for alpha channels. https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/833889aec024b792b1c5ce5089eaebc5eb45692f/core/io/image.cpp#L1962","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3874939293/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3942785204","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116065#issuecomment-3942785204","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116065","id":3942785204,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rAiC0","user":{"login":"fakemaxwell","id":59422275,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5NDIyMjc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59422275?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fakemaxwell","html_url":"https://github.com/fakemaxwell","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fakemaxwell/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fakemaxwell/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fakemaxwell/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fakemaxwell/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fakemaxwell/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fakemaxwell/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fakemaxwell/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fakemaxwell/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fakemaxwell/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-23T05:44:26Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T05:44:26Z","body":"More wrinkles- the initial test image is colored strokes on a grey background, making white pop if the transparent alpha pixels retain their white color.  With dark colors on top of dark colors and with black alpha pixels, the alpha outline created by mipmap generation appears as well:\n\n<img width=\"275\" height=\"283\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/295ca583-c5a2-4b26-bcb6-e091b2608966\" />\n<img width=\"304\" height=\"302\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c52e0363-a405-4324-a35a-8a2a4beca6fb\" />\n\nLeft is without mipmaps (same colors blend completely). Right is with mipmaps, creating the outline.  The dark outline tends to work fine in the context of most games- a barely noticeable outline on a 2d object against a background is rarely objectionable.  However as you can see here it can really affect the appearance, and far as I can tell the only answer is no mipmaps, which is real tough for a 2d game.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3942785204/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]